# Tab Grab

Tab Grab is a chrome extension that basically enhances Bookmarking, with more advanced organization features and requires less manual labor from the user.

Overall this project was created due to a problem that I faced constantly the past few years as an aspiring programmer. I constantly wished to learn more concepts
in programming, but my attention span was so low that I always procrastinated on focusing on the articles and videos I had opened up and proceeded to doomscroll. 
Overtime as I opened more and more articles, over the day without feeling the mood to read, I would reopen the following day ready to learn with so many articles
that I had to first organize in order to even start reading and researching. My first instinct was to use bookmarking in browser. However, bookmarking would ultimately
create an unorganized list that I would need lots of manual labor and thinking to organize into folders. That was overall my biggest problem. I decided to make an extension
that could solve that need of manual labor.

# API Key
Gemini API Key

# Key Features
- Right Clicking tab and clicking "Send to Dashboard" Will send a tab to your dashboard and will proceed to AI organize it into folders based on topics
- Auto tab closer and sorter that when you start a timer it will close automatically close tabs and send to dashboard after a timer has gone off.
- Summarizes individual tab's page content into a block of text.
- Able to manually create tabs and folders by yourself, includes editing tab and folder contents.

# Future features
- Flow chart(similar to Obsidian) connecting tabs based on relevance
- Chat bot

## Built With

- JavaScript
- HTML
- CSS
- Chrome Extension Manifest V3
- Node.js
- Express
- Google Gemini API
- Chrome Storage API
- Chrome Notifications API
- Render Free Server

### How to Download
1) Click the most recent release
2) Download the zip file and uncompress it
3) Go to manage your extensions(edge://extensions or chrome://extensions) and enter in developer mode.
4) Click load unpacked and select your uncompressed folder
5) YOUR GOOD TO GO!

***Warnings!!! Tab Grab is running on a Free Render server! So Tab grab may slow at sending tabs to your dashboard! If it isn't sent within a minute or two,
it means the gemini API is under going too many requests, and will require you to close and reopen your dashboard from your popup***

